From 182a690b79fabc32300871bc67b342bddc10818b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Rob Herring (Arm)" <robh@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 15:16:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: Fix phandle-array constraints, again

The unfortunately named 'phandle-array' property type is really a matrix
with phandle and fixed arg cells entries. A matrix property should have 2
levels of items constraints.

Acked-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260507201749.2605365-1-robh@kernel.org
Change-Id: I158a5f3f8d115d461eaa2daa686ebdb4e80b1023
Signed-off-by: Rob Herring (Arm) <robh@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 37534121c4e49a32e80d8a11de66fce25d448292)
Signed-off-by: Patrice Chotard <patrice.chotard@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/596847
Reviewed-by: Christophe KERELLO <christophe.kerello@st.com>
Domain-Review: Christophe KERELLO <christophe.kerello@st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
